## Change

- Added `MessageExtSubtype` hooks for Java's virtual `getPriority()` and
  `setPriority(int)` methods. The inherited getter continues through virtual
  `getProperty(PROPERTY_PRIORITY)`; the base setter retains the negative-value
  error and property write.
- The invoked Java direct-consume fixture overrides both priority methods,
  accepts `-7`, and compares the result, property view, and getter/setter
  counts. A second subtype overrides only `getProperty`; the fixture verifies
  inherited getter dispatch, base storage for priority `17`, and negative
  setter rejection.

